use rec was  remade for american audiences and  released is quarantined in 2008. wreck  was filmed in spain with the zombie  infused apartment building located on  ramla de catalunya a bustling street in  central barcelona  [Music]  similar to rodriguez balaguero was  working with a modest budget only two  million dollars okay so it's a lot more  than seven thousand but still for a  feature length film two million is not a  lot and with that modest budget  balaguero managed to make one of the  most terrifying horror films of all time  certainly in the found footage sub-genre  the bbc called it quote a runaway roller  coaster of a freight flick and empire  magazine wrote that it's a handheld  zombie flick with more than enough  shocks to hold its own wreck also  spawned a successful film series which  includes three sequels the latest of  which wreck iv apocalypse was released  in 2014. velasco's performance won her a  goya award for best new actress and for  those unfamiliar with the goya awards  they're essentially the oscars of spain  so this is a huge accomplishment but  still it doesn't make up for the fact  that you trapped her in an apartment  building filled with flesh-eating  zombies  roma  estonia  is  [Music]  [Music]  roma is set in mexico city in the 1970s  and follows live in housekeeper gleo one  of the two domestic workers who help  antonio and sophia an upper middle class  couple take care of their four children  now complications soon arise when  antonio runs away with his mistress and  cleo finds out that she's pregnant not  cool antonio sophia decides to take a  vacation with the kids and invites cleo  along for a much needed getaway to clear  her mind and bond with the family and  the film gets its name for being set in  the colonia roma neighborhood which is  where writer director alfonso cuaron  grew up in fact juaron has admitted that  roma was as autobiographical as it can  be adding that 90 comes out of his  memory and they actually shot in 